# SecAgent (agentic harness — MR review, analysis, Mattermost chat-ops) — Fedora/FIPS.
# Copy to /etc/secsuite/secagent.env and fill in the two secrets below. secdeploy seeds this
# file once (`test -f ... || install ...`) and never overwrites an existing one.
#
# Structured audit log (CMMC AU controls) — under this service's writable state dir
# (ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/secsuite/secagent). Fixed, not topology-derived, so it lives here
# rather than in the generated secagent-addressing.env.
SECAGENT_AUDIT__PATH=/var/lib/secsuite/secagent/audit/audit.jsonl
#
# 1. SecSSO service-account client secret (client_credentials, headless service identity —
#    "svc-secagent"). SecSSO's own operator provisions this value in SecSSO's .env; run
#    `./bootstrap/secsso.sh secagent-config` on the SecSSO host to confirm it's set there,
#    then paste the SAME value here (secdeploy has no cross-host way to fetch it — see
#    docs/fedora-fips.md#secagent-and-mattermost).
SECAGENT_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# 2. Mattermost bot token: run `./bootstrap/secchat.sh bot` on the SecChat host — it mints a
#    FRESH token and prints it ONCE ("copy the token value below"). Paste it here. Re-running
#    secchat.sh bot mints a NEW token every time (no "get or create"), so don't re-run it
#    once this is set without updating this file too.
SECAGENT_MATTERMOST__BOT_TOKEN=
#
# When topology.toml places SecRouter + SecSSO + SecChat (the collab tier's usual peers),
# secdeploy ALSO generates /etc/secsuite/secagent-addressing.env (SECAGENT_LLM__*,
# SECAGENT_SECSSO__TOKEN_URL/CLIENT_ID, SECAGENT_MATTERMOST__URL/TEAM/WEBHOOK_SECRET,
# SECAGENT_AUDIT__ENABLED) and layers it on top of this file via a second EnvironmentFile= in
# secagent.service — it wins over any of these keys it also sets. Don't hand-edit it; edit
# topology.toml and redeploy. See docs/fedora-fips.md#secagent-and-mattermost.
